          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6304346">sapien</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP404 Edworthy South

N 51° 03.153 W 114° 09.652&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My last BC find of the day.  It was funny to watch the GPSr count down as I approached GZ and then start counting right back up as I had to drove to find legal parking.  Fortunately the distance wasn't that far and the weather seemed to be holding out.  I wasn't sure which side of the barrier the cap was on; in the end, I found it on one side but had to do all my &quot;work&quot; from the other side because the cap was more accessible that way.  The park was busy but I don't think I attracted too much attention.  TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682803279">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP404 Edworthy Park South&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I've past this one so many times on my way by to walk dogs. Never noticed it before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks to Outforthehunt for maintaining the Brass Cap cache for everyone to enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;

